     "content": "This is an **exceptionally strong offer** for an L6 Product Manager at Google. \n\nSecuring a **$200,000 cash sign-on bonus** on top of a top-of-band **$1.08M equity grant** makes this a standout compensation package.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Numbers Breakdown\n\nAssuming standard Google front-loaded vesting (33% / 33% / 22% / 12%):\n\n| Component | Meta (Current IC6) | Google Revised Offer (Year 1) | Google Revised Offer (Year 2) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Base Salary** | $240,000 | $240,000 | $240,000 |\n| **Target Bonus** | $36,000 (15%) | $48,000 (20%) | $48,000 |\n| **Equity Vest** | ~$250,000 | **$356,400** *(33%)* | **$356,400** *(33%)* |\n| **Sign-on Bonus** | \u2014 | **$200,000** *(or split)* | \u2014 |\n| **Total Comp (Year 1)** | **~$526,000** | **~$844,400** | **~$644,400** |\n\n*Note: If Google splits the $200k sign-on over two years ($100k in Year 1 / $100k in Year 2), your compensation would be **~$744,400** in Year 1 and **~$744,400** in Year 2.*\n\nOver your first two years, you will make **~$1.48M to $1.5M total at Google**, compared to roughly **~$1.05M at Meta**\u2014an upside of over **$400,000+ in cold cash and liquid equity**.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Why You Should Accept\n\n1. **You fully eliminated the switching cost:** You asked for coverage of your $200k unvested Meta RSUs, and they gave it to you in **guaranteed cash** rather than future equity.\n2. **Top-Tier L6 Comp:** Total Year 1 comp of **~$840k+** (or ~$740k+ over 2 years) is near the absolute ceiling for a non-director/L6 PM in Big Tech.\n3. **No More Negotiating Leverage:** When Google offers a $200k sign-on and calls it their \"best and final,\" they have exhausted compensation committee approvals for this band. Pushing further risks souring the relationship or triggering an offer withdrawal.\n\n---\n\n### 3. A Few Practical Things to Check Before Signing\n\nBefore you put pen to paper, confirm these details with the recruiter:\n\n* **Sign-on Payout Structure & Clawback:** Confirm whether the $200,000 is paid out entirely in your first paycheck or split across Months 1 and 13. Also check the repayment/clawback terms (typically a prorated 12-month or 24-month retention commitment).\n* **Team & Scope:** Since you were happy at Meta, ensure you feel confident in the specific product area, your direct manager, and the engineering partner support for this L6 scope.\n\n---\n\n### Bottom Line\n\n**Yes, take the offer.** They fully matched your base, gave you top-band equity, and handed you $200,000 in cash to offset your unvested Meta stock. Congratulations on a textbook negotiation!",
